    "guidance": "Validated 0/12 under the fixed final-state exit rule; no reliable operating region was established, so do not select this policy by default. Its documented intended niche is after observed lid release, when a reachable peg displacement dominates, but that expected benefit is not confirmed by validation. Avoid early lid-held/phase-ambiguous states, large or wall-adjacent displacements, and any miss/drop/blocked-lift recovery. A first-pass event occurred transiently in 11/12 runs but was lost by the final state; all 12 finals had retrieve_peg_from_box=false, 8 retained an open cover and 4 ended closed, and 11/12 had IK-unconverged steps. Recognize failure from a low or stationary peg during lift, lack of stable peg/TCP co-motion, abrupt peg-to-TCP change, wall deflection, or repeated IK residual/limit contacts. Do not hand off on finger closure or a transient threshold crossing alone. Handoff to reorient_and_stage_peg only on closed fingers plus peg clearance and stable two-frame peg/TCP co-motion, with the scored terminal additionally requiring peg center >=0.15 m (or insertion) and cover >0.9 rad; no such final handoff was validated for this policy."
